[2026-06-26 13:01] ARCHITECT: Requirements: multi-tenant, real-time collab, block-based docs, conflict resolution, version history
[2026-06-26 13:01] ARCHITECT: System type: distributed collaborative workspace (Notion + Trello + Google Docs hybrid)
[2026-06-26 13:01] ARCHITECT: Constraint: eventual consistency only, no real WebSocket, in-memory

[2026-06-26 13:01] ARCHITECT: === ALTERNATIVE 1: EVENT-DRIVEN MODEL ❌ ===
  Как работает: все изменения → события в event log, subscribers apply events in order
  Pros: полный audit trail, easy to replay, familiar pattern
  Cons:
    - Total order requirement → single point of failure
    - Невозможно гарантировать order при network partitions
    - Conflict resolution: только last-write-wins (теряет данные)
    - Не подходит для offline-first (события могут прийти в любом порядке)
  Trade-off: хорошо для audit, плохо для collaborative editing
  Вердикт: ❌ REJECTED — не подходит для offline и concurrent editing

[2026-06-26 13:01] ARCHITECT: === ALTERNATIVE 2: CRDT-BASED MODEL ✅ ===
  Как работает: Conflict-free Replicated Data Type — каждый блок — CRDT
    - LWW-Register для text content
    - OR-Set для блоков документа
    - MV-Register для version tracking
  Pros:
    - No conflict resolution needed (mathematical guarantee)
    - Offline-first by design
    - Eventual consistency without coordination
    - Perfect for block-based editors
  Cons:
    - Сложность имплементации CRDT merge logic
    - Memory overhead (tomstone deletion)
    - Нужен garbage collection для deleted blocks
  Trade-off: сложность реализации vs математическая гарантия consistency
  Вердикт: ✅ SELECTED — единственный правильный выбор для collaborative editing

[2026-06-26 13:01] ARCHITECT: === ALTERNATIVE 3: LOCK-BASED MODEL ❌ ===
  Как работает: pessimistic locking — блок блокируется при редактировании
  Pros: простота, no conflicts
  Cons:
    - Невозможна real-time коллаборация
    - Deadlock risk
    - Плохой UX (wait for lock)
    - Offline невозможен
  Вердикт: ❌ REJECTED — антипаттерн для collaborative systems

[2026-06-26 13:01] ARCHITECT: === CRDT DEEP DIVE ===
  Block CRDT (position-based):
    - Block ID: UUID (уникальный, не зависит от порядка)
    - Position: fractional index (между соседями)
    - Content: LWW-Register (last-write-wins per character)
    - Deletion: tomstone (soft delete, GC later)

  Document CRDT:
    - OR-Set of blocks
    - Add: block appears
    - Remove: block tomstoned
    - Merge: union of sets

  Version tracking:
    - Hybrid Logical Clock (HLC) вместо Lamport
    - HLC = physical time + logical counter
    - Позволяет определить "happens-before" без синхронизации

[2026-06-26 13:01] ARCHITECT: === DATA MODEL ===
  Workspace: { id, name, tenants: [userId], blocks: Map<blockId, Block> }
  Block: { id, type, position, content, version, createdBy, createdAt, updatedAt, deleted }
  Tenant: { id, name, users: Map<userId, Role> }
  User: { id, name, role: 'owner' | 'editor' | 'viewer' }
  Event: { id, type, blockId, data, timestamp, userId, hlc }

[2026-06-26 13:01] ARCHITECT: === TRADE-OFFS ANALYSIS ===
  1. CRDT complexity vs eventual consistency guarantee → CRDT wins for collab
  2. Tombstone memory vs deletion simplicity → tomstone with periodic GC
  3. HLC vs Lamport clock → HLC gives physical time context
  4. Fractional index vs sequential → fractional allows O(1) insert
  5. In-memory vs persistent → in-memory ok for mock (requirement)
